          "date": "2026-11-04 17:34:39.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-17501 tests: count CPU partitions in conf-sanity 200",
        "message": "LU-17501 tests: count CPU partitions in conf-sanity 200\n\nOn a node with 2 NUMA nodes, conf-sanity test_200c fails:\n\n    CPU partitions not 2, found: 1\n\nThe cpu_partition_table output has 2 lines.  The test counts them\nwith \"echo $table | wc -l\".  The unquoted $table joins the lines\ninto one, so the count is always 1.  A VM with 1 NUMA node expects\n1 partition, so the bug does not show there.\n\nQuote the table in each partition count in test_200b and test_200c.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=200\nFixes: 111f5836ecbf (\"LU-17501 libcfs: allow CPT exclude list for cores\")\nFixes: d32cacd56129 (\"LU-17501 libcfs: extended range for exclude CPT pattern\")\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I8ed9b397333070e48f91fd575fdcc99c192fe835\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
